WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.740
Don't you see I'm cursed to this ship?

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.980
That's why I'm here.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.860
I think I know a way to break your curse.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.620
To free you from The Dutchman.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.040
Henry. No.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.080
I've read about a treasure.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.360
A treasure that holds all the power of the sea.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.060
The Trident of Poseidon can break your curse.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:20.260
Henry

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.800
The Trident can never be found.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.440
I found you!

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.700
It's just a tale.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.120
Like the tales of you and Captain Jack Sparrow?

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.960
He will help me find The Trident.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.700
You stay away from Jack.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.560
Leave the sea forever.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.800
You have to stop acting like a--

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.220
A pirate?

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.420
I wont stop.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.120
I want you to come home.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.340
Oh, hi Jack Sparrow.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.860
Jack Sparrow.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:56.920
Spanish?

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.620
You're, uh,  ghosts.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.880
Oh, they aren't able to step on land

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.520
I knew that though.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:11.980
Ghosts!

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.180
Help!

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:16.600
Carina!

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.900
You will soon pay for what you did to me.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.500
There's no need to bother, really.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.140
Carina!

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.840
I have no time to chat because my map just ran away.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.300
I will be waiting. For you.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.140
Why would you be waiting for me?

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:29.960
Why would he be waiting for me?

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.980
I'm looking for a pirate. Jack Sparrow.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.980
Bugger off.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:40.880
Psst. I need to speak with you.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.640
Hand me your sword.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:49.840
I don't have a sword.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.840
What kind of soldier has no weapon?

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.840
I'm currently wanted for treason.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.360
So not the very good kind then.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.240
I'm looking for a pirate, Captain Jack Sparrow.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.160
Well today is your lucky day.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.080
Cause I just happen to be

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:05.640
Captain

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:06.500
Jack

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.640
Sparrow

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.580
No, it can't be.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.880
I've spent years searching for...

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:17.840
this?

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.740
The great Jack Sparrow is not some drunk in a cell.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.960
Do you even have a ship? A crew?

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.400
Pants?

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.180
A great pirate does not require such intricacy.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.420
Do you know how long I've been waiting for this moment?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.560
The risks I've taken to be here.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.340
Are you sure you're the Jack Sparrow?

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.340
How would you like to die, pirate?

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.460
Hanging?

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.700
Firing squad?

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.540
Or a new invention?

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.340
The guillotine.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.040
Guillotine? Sounds French.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.840
I love the French. Did you know that they
invented mayonnaise?

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.260
How bad could it be, it's French eh?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.020
Oh.. very bad ..

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.360
Uh.. I've changed my mind!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.500
Here's an idea!

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:12.940
Here's an idea!

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.180
Why don't we try a good old-fashioned stoning, eh?

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.820
I'll kill Wisdon right now, gets the crowd involved, doesn't it?

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:23.660
I should like to speak to Victor in  Disembowelment! I should like to speak to him!

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.640
Pardon me.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:30.220
I, I'm not one complain normally but this basket's full of heads.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.670
 

